\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, O come, in pious lays 
\par Sound we God Almighty's praise'
\par Hither bring, in one consent,
\par Heart and voice and instrument :
\par Nor a creature dumb be found,
\par That hath either voice or sound.
\par \i 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i0\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Let those things which do not live
\par In still music praise give.      
\par \i0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come, ye sons of human race,
\par In this chorus take your place;
\par And amid the mortal throng
\par Be ye master of the song.
\par Let, in praise of God, the sound 
\par Run a never-ending round,
\par \i 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i0\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par That our song of praise may be
\par Everlasting, as is He
\par \i0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So, from heaven, on earth He shall
\par Let His gracious blessings fall;
\par And this huge wide orb we see 
\par Shall one choir, one temple be;
\par That our song may over-climb
\par All the bounds of place and time,
\par \i 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i0\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par And ascend from sphere to sphere
\par To the great Almighty's ear.
\par \lang1033\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

